act that someone with  bad intentions can track you and there's  nothing you can do about it is really  scary and really frustrating  apple says it's committed to air tax  privacy and security air tag is designed  with a set of proactive features to  discourage unwanted tracking if users  ever feel their safety is at risk they  are encouraged to contact local law  enforcement who can work with apple to  provide available information about the  unknown air tech inside edition anchor  deborah norville joins us right now uh  good morning hey so what do you do if  you get the alert on your phone that  there is an air tag well here's the  first thing you don't do you don't go  home you don't go to your office you  don't go to a place that you regularly  would go to because then you've just  given them all the information they need  the best thing to do is go to the police  station and say first of all if they're  tracking the police station they're not  going to come in there say i'm being  tracked there's an uh indication on my  phone that there is an air tag somewhere  in my person or on my car  can you help me and as the young woman  in atlanta who has it on her car she  went to the police the police said go to  apple apple said go to the police it's  like a cat chasing her tail she still  has this thing somewhere on her car  short of taking the car apart  they don't know how to find it and so  she has to wait for the battery to go  dead and the battery lasts for a year  yes that is he still doesn't know you  know that is such good advice you said  about don't go home because i think your  instinct is well let me go home and let  me call somebody so i think that's very  important to put that out there but  deborah how is it not illegal that  somebody could put a tracking device on  you and your car and your purse and your  coat and it and and that's okay that  that is not illegal so first of all this  is how small this thing is and you oh  it's glued down um you would